s=report.read_text().replace('97b91463d0b793cfe8650c26452a1dc736fbdf95d72966d5130163d19d366be9',h).replace('then appends191 lines','then appends193 lines')
s=s.replace('including the\noriginal six final-stop, ten pivot-stop and six observer-cause assertions and all\nneighbors,','including the\noriginal six final-stop assertions and all same-file neighbors,')
s=s.replace('The old\nfile already imports LinearAlgebra before the appended definitions. No import is\nadded.','The old\nLinearAlgebra import is inside module CrashLoggerTests and does not supply the new\ntop-level probe. The reviewed suffix explicitly adds `using LinearAlgebra:\nSingularException`, matching X\'s declared dependency. This source is NOT imported\nor executed during offline preparation.')
s += '''\n\n## Independent review correction (offline, no Julia)\n\nThe initial review rejected the candidate for an undeclared top-level SingularException\nbinding: the existing LinearAlgebra import was nested inside CrashLoggerTests. It also\nfound the misplaced coverage claim: ten pivot-stop and six observer-cause assertions are in\n`test/simplex_start_guard_tests.jl`, not the preserved start-state prefix. Both are\nImportant because they affect executable dependency closure and evidence scope.\nThe guard file remains unchanged and is reused historical coverage; no old test ran.\nThe frozen preparation plan's six/ten/six prefix wording is corrected by this explicit\nfile map; no historical plan or evidence is retroactively rewritten.\n\nOriginal candidate/append/source19/author10/pins1398 and review-initial remain preserved,\nSUPERSEDED/UNEXECUTED. The initial `no_new_import` and substring-only\n`native_import_already_available` checks are insufficient dependency evidence.\nOne separate correction adds only the explicit top-level dependency to the reviewed\nsuffix. Removing that exact insertion recovers the original suffix byte-for-byte;\nall50 assertions/core/defaults/copies/observations remain identical. Current canonical\nartifacts are candidate-reviewed.jl and append-reviewed.jl. Before-report/next-plan\ntexts preserve their old hash bindings; pins-reviewed supplies fresh read-time hashes.\nThe import introduces ordinary binding/module-loader work if first needed in a future\ncontext; it adds no explicit numerical call and proves no import-work/cache confinement.\nSource already declares the same dependency inside the untouched old module and X.\nNo Julia syntax/runtime qualification is claimed.\n'''
report.write_text(s)
p=plan.read_text().replace('97b91463d0b793cfe8650c26452a1dc736fbdf95d72966d5130163d19d366be9',h).replace('plus191 lines','plus193 lines').replace('Z report/review/candidate/source19/entry24/full read-time pins','Z report/review/candidate-reviewed/review-fix/source19/entry24/full reviewed read-time pins')
p += '\nCanonical Z candidate-reviewed.jl includes explicit top-level `using LinearAlgebra: SingularException`; the old module-scoped import is insufficient. Preserve it when extracting appended-only execution. Original rejected candidate/source19/author10 remain historical. Six final-stop assertions are in the preserved start-state prefix; ten pivot-stop and six observer-cause assertions are in unchanged start-guard tests, not that prefix. Before-review report/plan preserve initial1398/author8 bindings.\n'
plan.write_text(p)
green=dict(explicit_top_level_dependency=new.index(insert)<new.index('mutable struct'),correct_sibling_location='ten pivot-stop and six observer-cause assertions are in' in report.read_text())
checks=dict(two_RED=not any(red.values()),two_GREEN=all(green.values()),suffix_inverse=new.replace(insert,'',1)==old,prefix_exact=cand[:len(prefix)]==prefix,assertions50=new.count('@test checks.')==50,original_unchanged=sha(H/'candidate.jl')=='97b91463d0b793cfe8650c26452a1dc736fbdf95d72966d5130163d19d366be9',actual_test_unchanged=(R/'test/simplex_start_state_tests.jl').read_bytes()==prefix,no_new_numerical_call=new.count('JSimplex._crash_workspace(')==old.count('JSimplex._crash_workspace(')==1)
files=[H/'candidate-reviewed.jl',H/'append-reviewed.jl',H/'review_fix.py',H/'review-initial.md',report,plan,H/(report.name+'.before-review'),H/(plan.name+'.before-review')]
put(H/'review-fix.json',json.dumps(dict(RED=red,GREEN=green,checks=checks,all_passed=all(checks.values()),candidate_sha256=h,append_lines=len(new.splitlines()),sha256={str(p):sha(p) for p in files}),indent=2)+'\n');assert all(checks.values());print(json.dumps(dict(checks=checks,candidate=h,lines=len(new.splitlines()))))
